 the dragon ball super manga  the publisher will offer to pay another  mangaka to make a continuation instead  of gotoge  so in theory the original mangakao demon  slayer could make an incredible amount  of money  without even having to work on the  series any longer she could just move on  and work on some other series  and still profit off of someone else  working on the demon slayer sequel  now of course it is possible that the  mangaka might straight up say  no to both options with most people  if you offer them massive bags full of  money  they will eventually say yes but there  are people out there who might refuse  gotoge might just say hey i've made  enough money from demon slayer  i don't need anymore the publisher would  keep pushing though  they do not want to lose a profitable  series like this one  so soon but ultimately they may fail in  convincing the mangaka  still given the absolutely  record-breaking amount of profit the  demon slayer is generating  i am convinced that some type of  continuation is coming  it might be a sequel or a prequel or a  different story  in that same demon slayer world but i  think it's very likely  although i could be wrong so only time  will tell  whatever happens though i find the  prospect of some type of continuation  intriguing so for the rest of this video  i will talk about how the story itself  has left a ton of room for some form of  sequel  and i will explore some possibilities  for how the story might come back  if it indeed does from this point on the  video will contain  demon slayer manga spoilers so if you  are not caught up to the manga  this would be the time to click away all  you need to know is that demon slayer  is unbelievably popular and profitable  and because of that i am personally  confident that some type of sequel  is coming although nothing is confirmed  yet  okay now for all of us manga readers  here's how  i think the story could continue one  obvious way to continue the story would  be just